I'm **GamingBlur (@gamingblur on Discord)**, and I'm the **Team Lead for the UI/UX Team**.

Before continuing with this doc, please read the [General Onboarding Document](/guides/onboardings/general-onboarding/).

---

## What We Do

The UI/UX Team is responsible for designing and producing the game's interface assets, including menus, HUD elements, icons, dialogue boxes, and overall interface layout and flow, while keeping everything visually consistent, usable, and within the technical limits of the Nintendo DS.

In practice, that covers things like:

- Main menu, pause menu, other menus and settings screens
- HUD elements (health, status effects, maybe text fonts, etc.)
- Dialogue text boxes
- Battle & icons
- Other on-screen interface element that needs a consistent, readable style
- Website design

---

## Contributions

### Project Board

The board can be found here: [GitHub Project Board](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1), filtered to the "graphics" label.

1. Look under "Ready" for available tasks.
1. If a task is unassigned, assign it to yourself.
1. If a task is already assigned, message that person before joining. Multiple people can work on the same task together, but it should be coordinated first to avoid repeated work or style inconsistencies.
1. Move the task to “In progress”
1. Once you finish a task, move the task to “In Review” and share your work in #ui-ux-lounge for feedback.
1. Is there a task missing that you'd like to work on? Sure thing, but only if it's related to the UI/UX Team. Nothing for other teams should be added to this board. You can also take a look at the [Roadmap](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VUxY2xVGtKzGWCES0VeZ_-vMpKSifB5vTW2ZkXJMPJM/edit?usp=sharing) to see potential tasks to work on, but haven’t had a GitHub issue made yet!

### Task Assignment

- Always check the Project Board before starting a task, and only self-assign tasks that are unassigned.
- If a task is already assigned to someone else and you'd like to work on it too, message them first. More than one person can work on the same task, but it must be coordinated to avoid repeated work or noticeable style inconsistencies.
- New tasks may only be added to the board if they are directly related to the UI/UX Team's work (nothing belonging to other teams unless given permission)

### Communication

- Keep the team posted in #ui-ux-lounge on what you're working on, especially if you get stuck, get busy, or need to step away for a while. Radio silence is what causes problems.
- Life happens, and that's okay. Just tell us! If you go unresponsive or "ghost" the team without any communication for an extended period, you may be removed from the team and have your in-progress tasks reassigned. A quick “Hi guys, I’m not totally dead” avoids this.
- If you can no longer finish a task you've self-assigned, let the team know so it can be released back to the board for someone else.
- Share your progress and finished work in #ui-ux-lounge for feedback before considering a task complete.&nbsp; A second pair of eyes catches things you won't.

